b/PWA\nplatform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\ncriteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\nincidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\nmatter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\nnon-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n\n## Validation procedure\n\nBefore writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\nprovenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\nagainst the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n\n## Checkpoint and update procedure\n\nUpdate only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\nRetain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n\n## Stop condition\n\nStop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\n---\ntask_id: R0001\nsequence: 1\ntitle: Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\ndependencies:\nrequirement_ids: NFR-0010,NFR-0012\nsource_specifications: specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition,specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001\nauthoring_batch: B0001\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nAfter DEC-0001 selects the framework, package manager, and CI baseline, create\nthe smallest reproducible project skeleton for the shared game core, web\nadapter, and PWA adapter. Document one bootstrap, format, lint, and\ndeterministic test command interface, and make a clean approved-runtime\ncheckout run a deterministic sample test. This task establishes boundaries and\ntooling only; it does not implement game behaviour or resolve the decision.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThis is the first implementation contract and has no R-series dependencies.\nGATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained as a human implementation precondition:\nauthoring this runbook does not select a stack, and implementation must stop\nbefore selecting or installing framework, package-manager, or CI tooling.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- Root build and tooling configuration, including the pinned toolchain\n  declaration and command mapping.\n- `src/core/`, `src/content/`, `src/app/`, `src/platform/web/`, and\n  `src/platform/pwa/` ownership directories, created without feature code.\n- `tests/` and an isolated deterministic sample-test location.\n- `docs/development.md`, which records the approved-runtime bootstrap,\n  format, lint, and deterministic-test commands once DEC-0001 is decided.\n- The build/test command interface: `bootstrap`, `format`, `lint`, and\n  `test:deterministic` (or the selected tool's documented equivalent).\n\n## Behaviour\n\nUse the DEC-0001-approved runtime only. Pin its version and package-manager\nlock/metadata as appropriate to that approved selection. Create the isolated\ndirectory skeleton so later work has distinct shared-core, content, app,\nweb-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership.\n\nConfigure the selected tooling so the documented command interface has a\nsingle reproducible mapping for bootstrap, formatting, linting, and a\ndeterministic sample test. The sample test must use no wall clock, network,\nplayer data, browser storage, renderer, or platform feature. Record the exact\ncommands and a clean-checkout result in `docs/development.md`.\n\nThe skeleton must preserve the canonical direction: target adapters are\nseparate from the shared deterministic core, and no directory implies that a\ntarget may change campaign rules. Later R0002 owns enforcement of detailed\ncore/adapter dependency rules.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nThe responsive web and installable PWA targets receive separate adapter\ndirectories only. Neither adapter gains a renderer, service worker, cache\nlifecycle, browser API dependency, or target-specific campaign behaviour in\nthis task. PWA installation, caching, offline delivery, and update activation\nremain later scoped work; the PWA directory is an ownership boundary, not an\nimplementation of those features.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Deterministically validate creative coverage in a generated project.\n\nThis is a planning-quality gate, not product/release evidence.  It prevents a\nfactory from calling a game complete while the creative direction exists only\nas prose or is represented by a generic schema task.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\nID_PATTERNS = {\n    \"game\": re.compile(r\"\\bGAME-[A-Z0-9-]+\\b\"),\n    \"assets\": re.compile(r\"\\bASSET-[A-Z0-9-]+\\b\"),\n    \"audio\": re.compile(r\"\\bAUDIO-[A-Z0-9-]+\\b\"),\n    \"narrative\": re.compile(r\"\\bNAR-[A-Z0-9-]+\\b\"),\n}\n\n\ndef front_matter(path: Path) -> dict[str, str]:\n    document = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    match = re.match(r\"^---\\n(.*?)\\n---\\n\", document, re.DOTALL)\n    if not match:\n        return {}\n    result: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for line in match.group(1).splitlines():\n        key, separator, value = line.partition(\":\")\n        if separator:\n            result[key.strip()] = value.strip()\n    return result\n\n\ndef identifiers(path: Path, kind: str) -> set[str]:\n    return set(ID_PATTERNS[kind].findall(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))) if path.is_file() else set()\n\n\ndef values(value: object) -> list[str]:\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return [item for item in value if isinstance(item, str)]\n    if isinstance(value, str):\n        return [item.strip() for item in value.split(\",\") if item.strip()]\n    return []\n\n\ndef object_items(value: object) -> list[dict[str, object]]:\n    \"\"\"Return only JSON-object entries from a list-like field.\"\"\"\n    return [item for item in value if isinstance(item, dict)] if isinstance(value, list) else []\n\n\ndef is_game_workspace(workspace: Path) -> bool:\n    initial = workspace / \"INITIAL.md\"\n    return initial.is_file() and \"Game\" in initial.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef game_design_manifest_errors(workspace: Path, selected_modules: set[str], design_units: list[dict[str, object]]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Validate the deterministic handoff from generated G design work.\"\"\"\n    path = workspace / \"planning\" / \"game-design-manifest.json\"\n    if not path.is_file():\n        return [\"game is missing planning/game-design-manifest.json\"]\n    try:\n        manifest = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return [\"game-design-manifest.json is not valid JSON\"]\n    if not isinstance(manifest, dict):\n        return [\"game-design-manifest.json must be a JSON object\"]\n    errors: list[str] = []\n    audit = manifest.get(\"final_audit\")\n    if manifest.get(\"status\") != \"accepted\":\n        errors.append(\"game-design manifest status must be accepted\")\n    if not isinstance(audit, dict) or not isinstance(audit.get(\"task_id\"), str) or not audit[\"task_id\"].startswith(\"G\") or audit.get(\"status\") != \"accepted\":\n        errors.append(\"game-design manifest needs an accepted G-series final_audit\")\n    modules = {item.get(\"module\"): item for item in object_items(manifest.get(\"modules\")) if isinstance(item.get(\"module\"), str)}\n    for module in sorted(selected_modules):\n        entry = modules.get(module)\n        if not isinstance(entry, dict) or entry.get(\"status\") != \"accepted\":\n            errors.append(f\"game-design manifest has no accepted entry for selected module {module!r}\")\n            continue\n        if not values(entry.get(\"design_output_paths\")):\n            errors.append(f\"game-design manifest module {module!r} has no design output\")\n        covered = set(values(entry.get(\"game_design_ids\")))\n        required = {str(unit[\"id\"]) for unit in design_units if unit.get(\"module\") == module and isinstance(unit.get(\"id\"), str)}\n        if required and not required.issubset(covered):\n            errors.append(f\"game-design manifest module {module!r} does not cover its GAME-* units\")\n    if values(manifest.get(\"pending_modules\")) or values(manifest.get(\"blocked_modules\")):\n        errors.append(\"game-design manifest still has pending or blocked modules\")\n    return errors\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"project\", nargs=\"?\", help=\"Project name under projects/, or an absolute project workspace path. Defaults to the active Supervisor project.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--require-r-series\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Require every creative item to have a generated, required-media R contract.\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    root = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n    project_value = args.project\n    if not project_value:\n        database = Path(__import__(\"os\").environ.get(\"SUPERVISOR_DATABASE_PATH\", \"\"))\n        if database.name.endswith(\".sqlite3\") and database.parent.name == \".state\":\n            project_value = str(database.parent.parent)\n        else:\n            parser.error(\"project is required outside a Supervisor project run\")\n    workspace = Path(project_value).expanduser()\n    if not workspace.is_absolute():\n        workspace = root / \"projects\" / workspace\n    workspace = workspace.resolve()\n    specification = workspace / \"specification\"\n    catalogue_path = workspace / \"planning\" / \"implementation-catalogue-index.json\"\n    manifest_path = workspace / \"planning\" / \"runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"\n    errors: list[str] = []\n    if not catalogue_path.is_file():\n        errors.append(\"missing planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\")\n        catalogue: dict[str, object] = {}\n    else:\n        catalogue = json.loads(catalogue_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    contracts = {item.get(\"id\"): item for item in catalogue.get(\"contracts\", []) if isinstance(item, dict) and isinstance(item.get(\"id\"), str)}\n    coverage = catalogue.get(\"creative_coverage\", {})\n    if not isinstance(coverage, dict):\n        errors.append(\"creative_coverage must be an object\")\n        coverage = {}\n    expected = {\n        \"game\": identifiers(specification / \"02-game-design-bible.md\", \"game\"),\n        \"assets\": identifiers(specification / \"04-asset-direction.md\", \"assets\"),\n        \"audio\": identifiers(specification / \"04-audio-direction.md\", \"audio\"),\n        \"narrative\": identifiers(specification / \"02-narrative-content-model.md\", \"narrative\"),\n    }\n    selected_modules: set[str] = set()\n    design_units: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n    bible_json = specification / \"02-game-design-bible.json\"\n    if bible_json.is_file():\n        try:\n            payload = json.loads(bible_json.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            if not isinstance(payload, dict):\n                errors.append(\"02-game-design-bible.json must be a JSON object\")\n            else:\n        store.close()\n    return reopened\n\n\ndef _unmet_dependencies(runbooks: list[Path], states: dict[str, dict | None]) -> dict[str, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Return R tasks whose declared implementation dependencies are unaccepted.\"\"\"\n\n    available = {path.stem for path in runbooks}\n    unmet: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    for runbook in runbooks:\n        task = load_task(runbook)\n        missing = [dependency for dependency in task.dependencies if dependency not in available or (states.get(dependency) or {}).get(\"status\") != \"accepted\"]\n        if missing:\n            unmet[runbook.stem] = missing\n    return unmet\n\n\ndef _game_design_completion_error(workspace: Path, database_path: Path) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Return the durable G-series handoff failure, if a game is incomplete.\"\"\"\n    manifest_path = workspace / \"planning\" / \"game-design-manifest.json\"\n    if not manifest_path.is_file():\n        return \"missing planning/game-design-manifest.json\"\n    try:\n        manifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return \"game-design-manifest.json is not valid JSON\"\n    if not isinstance(manifest, dict) or manifest.get(\"status\") != \"accepted\":\n        return \"game-design manifest status is not accepted\"\n    audit = manifest.get(\"final_audit\")\n    if not isinstance(audit, dict) or not isinstance(audit.get(\"task_id\"), str) or audit.get(\"status\") != \"accepted\":\n        return \"game-design manifest has no accepted final_audit\"\n    if manifest.get(\"pending_modules\") or manifest.get(\"blocked_modules\"):\n        return \"game-design manifest still has pending or blocked modules\"\n    modules = manifest.get(\"modules\")\n    if not isinstance(modules, list) or not modules:\n        return \"game-design manifest has no completed modules\"\n    if any(not isinstance(module, dict) or module.get(\"status\") != \"accepted\" or not module.get(\"design_output_paths\") for module in modules):\n        return \"game-design manifest contains incomplete module evidence\"\n    bible_path = workspace / \"specification\" / \"02-game-design-bible.json\"\n    if not bible_path.is_file():\n        return \"missing specification/02-game-design-bible.json\"\n    try:\n        bible = json.loads(bible_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return \"02-game-design-bible.json is not valid JSON\"\n    if not isinstance(bible, dict):\n        return \"02-game-design-bible.json must be a JSON object\"\n    selected_modules = {value for value in bible.get(\"selected_modules\", []) if isinstance(value, str)}\n    if not selected_modules:\n        return \"game design bible has no selected modules\"\n    by_module = {entry.get(\"module\"): entry for entry in modules if isinstance(entry, dict) and isinstance(entry.get(\"module\"), str)}\n    if set(by_module) != selected_modules:\n        return \"game-design manifest modules do not exactly match selected game modules\"\n    design_units = [entry for entry in bible.get(\"design_units\", []) if isinstance(entry, dict)]\n    for module in selected_modules:\n        required_ids = {entry[\"id\"] for entry in design_units if entry.get(\"module\") == module and isinstance(entry.get(\"id\"), str)}\n        covered_ids = {value for value in by_module[module].get(\"game_design_ids\", []) if isinstance(value, str)}\n        if not required_ids or not required_ids.issubset(covered_ids):\n            return f\"game-design manifest does not cover selected GAME-* units for {module}\"\n    store = RunStore(database_path)\n    try:\n        state = store.state_for(audit[\"task_id\"])\n    finally:\n        store.close()\n    if (state or {}).get(\"status\") != \"accepted\":\n        return f\"G final audit {audit['task_id']} is not accepted in durable state\"\n    return None\n\n\ndef _run_ready_prerequisite_collections(\n    runbooks: list[Path], states: dict[str, dict | None], database_path: Path,\n    dry_run: bool, continue_on_nonpass: bool, repo_root: Path | None,\n) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Run project-local prerequisite collections once their task dependencies pass.\"\"\"\n\n    state_directory = database_path.parent\n    if state_directory.name != \".state\":\n        return True\n    workspace = state_directory.parent\n    known = {path.stem for path in runbooks}\n    for runbook in runbooks:\nCreate the matching machine-readable\n`planning/game-production-inventory.json`. Each entry identifies its design\nunit, selected module, content/design-card type, finite item or catalogue\nbatch, planned quantity, original brief, dependencies, asset/audio IDs,\nimplementation outcome, owner, and verification. Every selected module and\nevery `GAME-*` unit must have at least one inventory entry. A finite RPG roster\ntherefore names and describes its actual first-release party, bosses, towns,\nquests, or items as appropriate; a football-trivia catalogue instead has\nexplicit category/difficulty/type quotas and small editorial batches with\nsource validation. Do not use vague entries such as \u201cmake game content.\u201d\n\nFor a game, also create `projects/<project-slug>/game-design-runbooks/`, then\nwrite `GD0001.md`: a bounded game-design-programme dispatcher. Register this as\nthe `game-design-runbooks` project collection. It inherits the project's\nexisting `PROJECT_BRIEF.md` and `INITIAL.md`; never create or duplicate an\n`INITIAL.md` inside this collection.\nGD0001 reads the discovery, identity, initial design bible, creative direction,\nand production inventory; it writes `planning/game-design-manifest.json` and\ncreates at most ten `GB` bounded design-runbook writers, one `GC` catalogue\ncheckpoint, and one successor `GD` dispatcher when more work remains. Each\n`GB` writer creates at most **five** focused `G` design runbooks. Those G files\ncreate/review the detailed bibles required by the selected modules (not a fixed\nRPG list), such as story/world/party/boss design for an RPG or question\nbank/scoring/fairness design for trivia. `GC` validates G ownership, design-unit\ncoverage, dependency closure, output quality, and manifest consistency before a\nlater GD wave continues. GD dispatchers add further bounded waves until every\nrequired design module and production entry has completed design evidence, then\ncreate a final `GQ` design audit.\nThe final audit must update the canonical bible and inventory, run the\ndedicated manifest completion check, and leave a completed manifest. The full\nimplementation-coverage validator runs later, after F012 creates its catalogue.\nDo not generate B or R implementation runbooks until the G collection has\npassed.\n\nThe manifest is a completion gate, not a prose report. Its required fields are\n`status: accepted`, `final_audit` (`task_id: G...`, `status: accepted`), and a\n`modules` array. Each selected module records `module`, `status: accepted`,\n`design_output_paths`, `game_design_ids`, and `production_inventory_ids`.\nIt also records empty `pending_modules` and `blocked_modules` arrays. The final\naudit may set these values only after it has checked all generated G evidence;\nthe Supervisor and `scripts/runbookgen validate` reject any other form. The\nmanifest module set must exactly match `02-game-design-bible.json`, and each\nmodule must cover all of its canonical `GAME-*` design-unit IDs before F006 can\nstart.\n\nEvery generated `G0001`, `G0002`, \u2026 design task uses normal Supervisor task\nmetadata and declares `design_authoring_batch: GB0001` (or its actual GB\nwriter). G tasks are the actual game-design work; GB/GC/GD/GQ files are only\nthe scalable authoring, checking, dispatch, and audit layer that lets hundreds\nof detailed G files be created without a single giant prompt.\n\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' runbooks/TEMPLATE.md; find projects/football-trivia-e2e -maxdepth 2 -type f -name '*manifest*.json' -o -name '*checkpoint*.json'; rg -n 'design_authoring_batch|gam